# No Magic Values

**Never use magic numbers or strings directly in code.** All values must be extracted under `lib/src/core/constants/` and imported as named constants.

## Hierarchy (ULLR-99)

```
lib/src/core/constants/
├── constants.dart   # Barrel
├── http/            # Status codes, HTTP debug knobs
├── auth/            # Auth config, JSON keys, login copy
├── api/             # ULLR paths, Maps fields, response keys
├── app/             # Routes, colors, dimensions, env, branding
├── features/        # Dashboard, gear, weather, settings, messages
└── dev/             # Dev auto-login and tooling flags
```

Prefer a specific library import (optionally with `show`) or `package:ullr_mobile/src/core/constants/constants.dart`.

### ❌ Bad Examples:
```dart
if (status == 'OK') { /* ... */ }
await dio.get('/weather');
```

### ✅ Good Examples:
```dart
import 'package:ullr_mobile/src/core/constants/http/http_status.dart';
import 'package:ullr_mobile/src/core/constants/api/api_config.dart';

if (status == ApiResponseStatus.ok) { /* ... */ }
await dio.get(UllrApiPaths.weather);
```

## When to Extract Constants

Extract any value that has semantic meaning, appears in multiple places, might change, or represents business/config logic (status strings, API paths, UI copy, weather codes, timeouts, feature flags).

## Code Review Checklist

- [ ] No unexplained numbers (except 0, 1, -1 in simple cases)
- [ ] No hardcoded strings in business logic / UI copy
- [ ] New constants land in the correct subdomain folder
- [ ] Class/member names are descriptive (`UPPER_SNAKE` for values inside classes as today)
